    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Periodic adult preventive visit before a multi-year Arctic expedition. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Sir John is a 58-year-old naval officer with stage 2 hypertension on amlodipine, class 1 obesity, mild noise-induced hearing loss and vitamin D insufficiency on vitamin D3, who is preparing to command an Arctic expedition expected to last two to three years, and comes for his preventive visit two weeks after his four-week review. He has recovered from influenza except for a dry cough on cold mornings, and he walks three to four miles a day again. His home readings this week average 131/81. He has lost 2.4 kg since intake by walking, hill climbing and smaller portions. His dentist examined him last week, took films and replaced a cracked filling. He had influenza and COVID-19 vaccines in the autumn and his last tetanus booster was more than ten years ago; he has never had pneumococcal, zoster, hepatitis B or rabies vaccines. He has never had colorectal cancer screening. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 58, nine weeks before sailing</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Home average 131/81 on amlodipine 5 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>88.4 kg, from 90.8 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Amlodipine 5 mg daily; vitamin D3 25 micrograms daily</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on paper in the waiting room and reviewed with him by Dr. Ashby-Nwankwo. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good; better since the influenza passed</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Married; busy with the expedition&apos;s preparations; the end of his last post still weighs on him, and he sees the command as a chance to set that right</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>One glass of wine with dinner on most days, down from two; AUDIT-C 3 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks three to four miles a day, with hills twice a week</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Smaller portions, more vegetables and fruit, less salt and fewer puddings</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven hours; no snoring reported, no daytime sleepiness</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt; no firearms at home; uses hearing protection on the gun deck</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Trouble hearing in noisy rooms; reading glasses; eye examination last year</td></tr><tr><td>Oral health</td><td>Dental examination and a replaced filling last week</td></tr><tr><td>Travel</td><td>Two to three years in the Arctic with no outside contact; ship&apos;s surgeons on board; no evacuation possible for months at a time</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

