  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated for an expedition beyond the reach of care. Tuberculosis blood test at intake negative. Lipids reviewed at intake; he chose no statin for now. [S]<list><item>Tdap, PCV20, recombinant zoster (first dose), hepatitis B (first dose) and rabies pre-exposure prophylaxis (first dose) today.</item><item>Second rabies dose with the nurse in one week; second hepatitis B dose at the eight-week review; second zoster dose at the pre-departure visit.</item><item>Fecal immunochemical test kit given; HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening drawn before the hepatitis B vaccine.</item><item>Next preventive visit on his return.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential hypertension on amlodipine (I10)</content>. Home average 131/81, close to goal. [S]<list><item>Continue amlodipine 5 mg; eight-week review.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>132/80 mmHg; treated hypertension</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening and cardiovascular risk</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Lipid panel at intake; PREVENT 10-year cardiovascular risk about 6 percent; statin discussed and declined for now</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>HbA1c 5.6% at intake; recheck on return</td></tr><tr><td>Obesity counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>His own plan of walking, hills and smaller portions reviewed; 2.4 kg lost</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Never screened; fecal immunochemical test today, as colonoscopy cannot be fitted in before sailing; colonoscopy if positive</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>For men 65 to 75 who have ever smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Declined</td><td>Shared decision-making at 55 to 69; he chose not to have a PSA test</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Once for adults to 65; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Once for all adults; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Triple panel once for all adults; drawn before the first vaccine dose</td></tr><tr><td>Latent tuberculosis screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Interferon-gamma release assay negative at intake, after a household contact long ago</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Up to date</td><td>AUDIT-C 3 at intake; cutting back</td></tr><tr><td>Dental examination</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Examined with films last week; a cracked filling replaced; no other work needed before sailing</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap today; last booster more than ten years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 today, recommended from 50; no further dose needed</td></tr><tr><td>Zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First recombinant dose today; second before departure</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First HepB-CpG dose today; second in four weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Rabies pre-exposure prophylaxis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First dose today, second in seven days; for years in the Arctic beyond the reach of rabies immune globulin</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Given last autumn; next doses on his return</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended at 50 to 74 only with conditions that raise risk; none</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tetanus, diphtheria and acellular pertussis (Tdap) booster; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine (PCV20), single dose; Recombinant zoster vaccine, first of two doses; Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), first of two doses; Rabies vaccine (human diploid cell), pre-exposure prophylaxis, first of two doses [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Use of a Modified Preexposure Prophylaxis Vaccination Schedule to Prevent Human Rabies: Recommendations of the Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices, United States, 2022 (2022); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Colorectal Cancer: Screening (2021); Prostate Cancer: Screening (2018); Screening and Testing for Hepatitis B Virus Infection: CDC Recommendations — United States, 2023 (2023); Universal Hepatitis B Vaccination in Adults Aged 19-59 Years: Updated Recommendations of the Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices, United States, 2022 (2022); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Second rabies dose with the nurse in one week. Fecal test and screening results by phone. Eight-week review with the exercise treadmill test and the second hepatitis B dose. Next scheduled visit 1845-04-07: eight-week review: blood pressure at goal, weight, exercise treadmill test and expedition planning. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
